            "confidence": 0.95,
            "description": "#### Description\nLines 39\u201341 define Compose-interpolation defaults for the database credentials: [REDACTED-SECRET], DB_USER, and DB_PASSWORD all fall back to the string 'widgetshop'. The password is therefore identical to the username, trivially guessable, and committed in plaintext to source control. Because the db service uses `expose` (not `ports`), the port is not reachable from the host, but every container in the default Compose bridge network (api, migrate, and any future service) can connect to db:5432 with these well-known credentials. An attacker who achieves code execution in the api container \u2014 for example by exploiting an injection flaw in the Express layer \u2014 can immediately pivot to a full database dump with `psql -h db -U widgetshop -d widgetshop`.\n\n#### Impact\nAny process that can reach db:5432 on the Docker network \u2014 including a compromised API container \u2014 can authenticate to PostgreSQL using credentials published in the repository. The entire database (users, orders, payment tokens, PII) is exposed once one container in the stack is breached.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\n1. Attacker exploits an injection or RCE bug in the Express API container. 2. From that shell, they run `PGPASSWORD=[REDACTED-SECRET] psql -h db -U widgetshop widgetshop -c '\\copy users to stdout'`. 3. Because the password is the published default and was never overridden in the deployment .env, authentication succeeds and the full users table is exfiltrated. No brute-force required \u2014 the credential is in the public repository.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- The .env file (loaded via env_file) does not define DB_PASSWORD, so the Compose default 'widgetshop' is used\n- Attacker has achieved code execution inside at least one container on the same Compose network (e.g., api)\n\n```\n      POSTGRES_DB: ${DB_NAME:-widgetshop}\n      POSTGRES_USER: ${DB_USER:-widgetshop}\n      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${DB_PASSWORD:-widgetshop}\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nRemove the weak literal default entirely: change line 41 to `POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${DB_PASSWORD}` (no fallback). This forces operators to supply a secret explicitly and causes Compose to refuse to start if the variable is absent, making misconfiguration visible at startup time rather than at breach time. Rotate the credential on any deployment that ran with the default. Store the real value in a secrets manager or a .env file excluded from version control.\n\n**Exploitability:** CVSS 8.1. AV:A limits direct internet reachability, but every Compose service is on the same bridge network. The committed 'widgetshop'/'widgetshop' default makes Postgres accessible to any attacker who achieves code execution in the api container. Full dump of PII, credential hashes, order history, and card tokens in a single psql session. Unlocked by finding 6 or any injection flaw in the Express layer.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 7/10) \u2014 Compose-interpolation fallback `POSTGRES_PASSWORD:-widgetshop` is committed and differs from `.env.example`'s `change-me`; no `.env` exists in repo; pivot from the `api` container to a full DB dump requires only the well-known credential, no brute-force.\n\nI now have everything needed to render a verdict. Let me consolidate the evidence:\n\n**What the code actually does (verified):**\n- `docker-compose.yml` line 41: `POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${DB_PASSWORD:-widgetshop}` \u2014 confirmed verbatim.\n- The `db` service uses `expose` (not `ports`), so port 5432 is on the internal Compose bridge only.\n- The `api` and `migrate` services specify `env_file: .env`, but the `db` service does NOT \u2014 it only uses the `environment:` block with Compose interpolation.\n- Compose variable interpolation also reads a root-level `.env` file, so if one exists, `${DB_PASSWORD}` is satisfied from there and the `:-widgetshop` fallback is skipped.\n\n**The `.env` situation:**\n- `.gitignore` excludes `.env` \u2014 it is **not committed**.\n- `.env.example` IS committed and uses `DB_PASSWORD=change-me` (not `widgetshop`).\n- No `.en\u2026"
          },
