            "description": "#### Description\nAt line 9, `q` is read directly from `req.query` with no sanitisation. At line 12, it is interpolated into the template literal `` `%${q}%` `` and passed to `andWhereILike`. Knex binds the resulting string as a prepared-statement parameter (no SQL injection), but the PostgreSQL engine still interprets `%` and `_` inside the bound LIKE pattern as wildcards. A value like `q=%` matches every row (equivalent to no filter, but still forces an ILIKE scan). A crafted pattern such as `q=%a%b%c%d%e%f%g%h%` with many alternating literals forces the ILIKE engine into a multi-pass scan for each row. Because the route has no authentication middleware and no rate limit visible in this slice, an attacker can issue rapid-fire requests to keep the database worker threads busy.\n\n#### Impact\nAn unauthenticated caller can supply SQL LIKE metacharacters (`%`, `_`) in the `?q=` parameter. While the value is correctly passed as a bound parameter (no SQL injection), the unescaped wildcards are evaluated by the database engine, enabling an attacker to craft patterns that force the database to perform a full sequential scan of the widgets table on every request. Sustained abuse can degrade query latency for all users.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nAn attacker sends repeated GET requests to `http://<host>/api/catalog/widgets?q=%25a%25b%25c%25d%25e%25f%25g%25h%25` (URL-encoded `%a%b%c%d%e%f%g%h%`). Each request forces an ILIKE multi-segment scan across the widgets table. Without rate limiting or query timeout, concurrent requests from a low-bandwidth client can saturate the database connection pool and increase p99 latency for legitimate shoppers.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- No authentication or rate-limiting on the GET /widgets endpoint (no auth middleware is applied in this file)\n- Widgets table is sufficiently large for scan cost to be significant\n\n```\n  const { category_id, q } = req.query;\n  let query = db('widgets').where({ is_active: true });\n  if (category_id) query = query.andWhere({ category_id });\n  if (q) query = query.andWhereILike('name', `%${q}%`);\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nEscape LIKE metacharacters in `q` before embedding them in the pattern. Replace `%` with `\\%` and `_` with `\\_`, then pass `\\` as the ESCAPE character: `query.andWhereRaw('name ILIKE ? ESCAPE ?', [\\`%${escapedQ}%\\`, '\\\\'])`. Additionally, enforce a maximum length on `q` (e.g. 100 characters) and apply a request rate-limit middleware to the catalog routes.\n\n**Exploitability:** CVSS 5.3. Pre-auth, AC:L. Knex binds the LIKE pattern as a prepared-statement parameter (no SQL injection), but Postgres still processes wildcard semantics inside the bound value. Crafted patterns with many alternating wildcards force catastrophic ILIKE backtracking per row. No rate-limiting on the catalog endpoint. Moderate standalone DoS; contributes to the inventory-exhaustion chain by inducing payment timeouts that prevent stock restoration.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 9/10) \u2014 code confirmed as described; route is unauthenticated with no rate-limit or query timeout; unescaped LIKE wildcards in the bound parameter force expensive per-row ILIKE scans that a low-bandwidth attacker can sustain to saturate the DB connection pool\n\n**Analysis**\n\n**A. Establish the call chain**\n\nThe graph context is sparse (no callers listed). I fell back to source tracing.\n\n**app.js line 23:**\n```js\napp.use('/api', catalogRoutes);\n```\nNo auth middleware wraps this mount. `requireAuth` exists in `auth.js` but is not applied here.\n\n**B. Confirm the sink code (catalog.js:9-12)**\n\nThe file content matches the scanner's snippet exactly:\n```js\nconst { category_id, q } = req.query;          // line 9 \u2014 raw from URL\nlet query = db('widgets').where({ is_active: true });\nif (category_id) query = query.andWhere({ category_id });\nif (q) query = query.andWhereILike('name', `%${q}%`);  // line 12 \u2014 q interpolated in\n```\nKnex passes `%${q}%` as a bound parameter \u2192 **no SQL injection**, confi\u2026"
